{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"6d77d2d4-2d57-4324-b9fb-8a5da0b39871","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Here’s what was changed to fix the cache‑eviction problem caused by `save_fact` writes:\n\n- **`bot.py` – `build_system` function** now creates **two** cached blocks instead of one:\n  1. **Static instructions** (`INSTRUCTIONS`) – never changes, marked with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`.\n  2. **Volatile per‑user tail** (`athlete_context(a, today)`) – includes date, profile, zones, goal, facts, etc., also marked `ephemeral` but this is the only part that changes when a fact is saved.\n\n- The function now returns a list of the two blocks, each with its own `cache_control` marker, so a memory write only invalidates the tail while the static prefix stays hot.\n\nThe detailed explanation and the parts of the colleague’s note that were applied are recorded in the artifact:\n\n**[ANSWER.md](/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6d77d2d4-2d57-4324-b9fb-8a5da0b39871/ANSWER.md)**\n\nFeel free to run the bot and check `logs/usage.jsonl` to confirm that after a `save_fact` only the tail block is recreated (smaller `cache_creation_input_tokens`), while the static block continues to be read from cache.\n","duration_seconds":49.596063,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":17862,"output_tokens":2607,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":103296,"total_tokens":20469}}}
